Since \int_0^2 x^k dx=\frac{2^{k+1}}{k+1}, the sum equals \int_0^2 (\frac{(1+x)^{12}+(1-x)^{12}}{2}-1) dx
Integrating gives \frac{3^{13}-1+2}{26}-2=\frac{3^{13}-51}{26}
Comparison with \frac{3^{13}-\alpha}{26} gives \alpha=51 → (C)

