Dotting with \vec{a} and using \vec{a}\cdot\vec{a}=26, \vec{a}\cdot\vec{b}=35, \vec{a}\cdot\vec{c}=15 gives k=\frac{1}{5}
Hence \vec{c}\cdot(\hat{i}+\hat{j}-3\hat{k})=\frac{2}{3}(-6)-\frac{1}{15}(15)=-5 → (B)

9016:
Factorising x^4+x^2+1=(x^2+x+1)(x^2-x+1) cancels \sqrt{x^2+x+1} leaving \frac{\sqrt{x}}{\sqrt{x+1}\sqrt{x^2-x+1}}=\frac{\sqrt{x}}{\sqrt{x^3+1}}
With x=t^2, dx=2t dt the integral becomes \int_0^{\sqrt{2}}\frac{2t^2}{\sqrt{t^6+1}}dt=\frac{2}{3}\int_0^{2\sqrt{2}}\frac{du}{\sqrt{u^2+1}} via u=t^3
Evaluating gives \frac{2}{3}\ln(2\sqrt{2}+3)=\frac{2}{3}\ln(3+2\sqrt{2}) → (C)

