Hence g(x)=\frac{1}{x}; it meets y=x-\frac{3}{2} at x=2 while the line meets y=0 at x=\frac{3}{2}
Adding the triangle \int_{3/2}^2(x-\frac{3}{2})dx=\frac{1}{8} and \int_2^4\frac{dx}{x}=\ln 2 gives \frac{1}{8}+\ln 2 → (A)

